# Project Setup Runbook — Claude SDK + AWS Bedrock + Azure Key Vault

You are helping April set up a Python project that uses Claude Code with two
provider options (enterprise SSO and AWS Bedrock) and pulls credentials from
Azure Key Vault. Walk through this step by step. Run commands, check output,
and move on only when each step succeeds. If something fails, fix it before
continuing.

**Do not make changes until April says "go" or "lets begin" or similar.** Read
this file first, understand the full plan, then summarise what you will do and
wait for her confirmation.

---

## Context — April's environment

- **OS:** Windows 10/11, PowerShell
- **Python:** 3.11+ managed with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- **Claude CLI:** installed via `winget install --id Anthropic.ClaudeCode`
- **Auth:** Enterprise Claude via SSO (primary), AWS Bedrock (secondary)
- **AWS auth:** Okta SAML federation — temporary credentials from CloudShell
- **AWS account:** `<your-security-account>` (<ACCOUNT_ID>)
- **IAM role:** `<your-cybersecurity-role>`
- **AWS region:** `us-east-1`
- **Azure Key Vault:** `<your-keyvault>` at `https://<your-keyvault>.vault.azure.net/`
- **Azure tenant:** GeneLabs (`36eae5cd-e5ad-4ea6-9d47-86fca48c4841`)

