## Phase 1 — Prerequisites (verify, don't install blindly)

### 1.1 Claude CLI

```powershell
claude --version
```

If not found: `winget install --id Anthropic.ClaudeCode`, restart terminal.

### 1.2 Claude login

```powershell
claude auth status
```

If not logged in:

```powershell
claude login
```

It opens a browser for SSO. After authenticating, verify with `claude auth status`.
You should see `"loggedIn": true`. The `apiProvider` may say `bedrock` if the project
has `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1` in settings — that is fine and will be handled in
Phase 3.

### 1.3 Workspace trust

Run Claude Code interactively once in the project directory:

```powershell
claude
```

Accept the trust dialog when prompted, then `/exit`. This is a one-time step that
enables the permission rules in `.claude/settings.json`. Without it, Claude Code
ignores all `permissions.allow` entries.

**How to tell if trust is already set:** Run `claude -p "hello"`. If you see
"Ignoring N permissions.allow entries... workspace has not been trusted", trust is
not set.

### 1.4 AWS CLI

```powershell
aws --version
```

If not found but installed, add to PATH:

```powershell
$env:Path += ";C:\Program Files\Amazon\AWSCLIV2"
```

If not installed: `winget install --id Amazon.AWSCLI` (admin PowerShell), restart
terminal.

### 1.5 Azure CLI

```powershell
az --version
```

If not found: `winget install --id Microsoft.AzureCLI` (admin PowerShell).

Verify login:

```powershell
az account show
```

If not logged in: `az login`. Should show `<you>@genelabs.example` on the GeneLabs
tenant.

### 1.6 uv

```powershell
uv --version
```

If not found: `winget install --id astral-sh.uv`.

