## Phase 3 — Claude Code settings

### 3.1 Create `.claude/settings.json`

This file controls permissions and the provider mode. Start in **enterprise mode**
(Bedrock off) so it works immediately with SSO.

**Create `.claude/settings.json` with this content:**

```json
{
  "_comment": "Non-secret project settings. Bedrock is OFF - using enterprise Claude account via SSO.",
  "env": {},
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Read(**)",
      "Edit(**)",
      "Bash(python:*)",
      "Bash(python3:*)",
      "Bash(soffice:*)",
      "Bash(ls:*)",
      "Bash(mkdir:*)",
      "Bash(cp:*)",
      "Bash(aws bedrock list-inference-profiles:*)",
      "Bash(aws sts get-caller-identity:*)",
      "WebFetch",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_search_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_get_*",
      "mcp__splunk-mcp-server__splunk_run_query",
      "mcp__shodan__*",
      "mcp__nvd__*",
      "mcp__intel471__*",
      "mcp__threatq__*",
      "mcp__rapid7__*",
      "mcp__enrich__*",
      "mcp__claroty__*",
      "mcp__search__*"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Bash(rm:*)",
      "Bash(git push:*)",
      "Bash(curl:*)",
      "Bash(wget:*)",
      "Bash(aws bedrock-runtime invoke-model:*)",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_add_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_update_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_delete_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_create_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_perform_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_execute_*",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_init_rtr_session",
      "mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_run_rtr_*"
    ]
  },
  "_model_note": "Using enterprise Claude account via SSO. Latest models available. Switch: .\\switch_provider.ps1 bedrock"
}
```

**Adapt the `permissions` block for this repo.** The MCP server names above are for
the CTI scanner's nine connectors. If this repo has different MCP servers, update the
allow list to match `.mcp.json`. Keep the deny list — it prevents destructive
operations.

The example allow list is intentionally broad. The full CTI hunting setup needs these
additional entries beyond the template above (add to match `.mcp.json`):

```json
"mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_aggregate_*",
"mcp__falcon-mcp__falcon_check_connectivity",
"mcp__splunk-mcp-server__splunk_run_saved_search",
"mcp__splunk-mcp-server__splunk_get_info",
"mcp__ics-advisories__*"
```

Drop `"mcp__search__*"` if no search MCP server is configured.

### 3.2 Verify Claude Code works in enterprise mode

```powershell
claude -p "Say hello and confirm which model you are. One sentence."
```

Expected: a response from the latest Claude model (e.g. Opus 5) with no errors.

If you get "Could not load credentials from any providers", Claude CLI is pointed at
Bedrock but has no AWS creds. The fix is Phase 3.1 above — make sure `"env": {}` is
empty (no `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK`).

